/*
  KG-QL: Process-Dynamics Illuminance Controller Agent

  JaCaMo project file for the Gradle task "taskDynamics".

  Starts one BDI agent, illuminance_controller_agent_dynamics
  (src/agt/illuminance_controller_agent_dynamics.asl), which learns the response
  delay of each actuator instead of a Q-table.

  To run: ./gradlew taskDynamics -Pprofile=lab2_slow -Pmode=ql_true
          (while the matching SLOW Node-RED simulator flow is running:
           lab2_slow -> port 1895, lab3_slow -> port 1896)

  The agent probes every actuator to learn its response delay (fast task lamp
  ~0 ticks; slow motorized blind ~12 ticks), writes the learned ws:responseDelay
  values to a separate Turtle file (no program reads it back), and then uses
  the measured delays, held in memory, to satisfy time-bounded goals ("reach the target illuminance within D seconds").

  Options:
    -Pprofile=<id>   Slow lab profile (system property active.profile).
    -Pmode=ql_true   Knowledge-guided planner: uses the learned per-actuator delay.
    -Pmode=ql_false  Plain planner: assumes zero delay (no dynamics knowledge).
                     The mode is passed as the system property dynamics.mode.
*/

mas lab_dynamics {

    agent illuminance_controller_agent_dynamics

}
